# 📅 September — A Fresh Start

The halls smell like new sneakers and anxiety. It's the first week of Grade 12 and everything feels manageable — even exciting.

Your teachers are upbeat but firm. In English, Mr. Hargrove holds up his hand before anyone can speak.

*"This year, I want you to do your own thinking. There are tools out there that will try to do it for you. Don't let them. Your mind is the only thing that's truly yours."*

You nod along with everyone else. Seems easy enough.

